// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2542204397" "Kings Row briefing"
// DetailString :
"P2788616626" "A lot of hardworking folks live in Kings Row, home to most of Paragon City's labor force.  The place was named after the King Garment Works, but that business went under over twenty years ago.  Now, Kings Row is in the hands of all sorts of businesses, from small factories to various Crey subsidiaries.  Unfortunately, those damn Skulls have taken over the streets.  Some people say that those ghouls belong to some sort of death cult.  Whether that's true or not, the Skulls are sure full of trouble."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1270955349" "I need you to get over to the Kings Row Security Chief right away.  Follow your compass."
// AcceptString :
"P3342708256" "See Kings Row Security Chief"
// SendOffString :
"P1136267895" "There have been reports of some trouble with the Skulls in Kings Row, so he may send you after them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3591996871" "Talk to Security Chief"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3580910434" "Get over to the Security Chief as soon as possible."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2353597473" "This briefing will help you.  Now get out there and take out those Skulls.  You might try looking for them in High Park or Freedom Plaza."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1634651953" "Keep the peace in Kings Row"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1743655708" "Kings Row is like a war zone right now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P221487368" "You have defeated 10 Skulls."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3007238318" "The security force sends their thanks.  Good work, {HeroName}!  It won't be easy to clean up Kings Row, but with your help, we have a much better chance of success."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1834910498" "Perez Park briefing"
// DetailString :
"P2188376604" "Perez Park used to be a beautiful place to take your family for an afternoon picnic.  Now no one in his right mind wanders in there.  Most of the area has been abandoned, largely due to the rumors of unholy Circle of Thorns rites taking place deep within the forest.  The park is entirely overgrown, a perfect place for those strange mystics to summon up a demon or two. <color orange>This zone is so deadly that even Heroes shouldn't go in there in groups of fewer than three.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2105416679" "The Security Chief for Perez Park asked for you by name.  You should take that as a compliment.  Go talk to him.  He's located in Atlas Park near the gates to Perez Park."
// AcceptString :
"P1634935775" "See Perez Park Security Chief"
// SendOffString :
"P2695910350" "Perez Park is a dangerous place these days.  </color orange>Clearly the Chief thinks you can handle it, but take a couple friends with you, just in case.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1806100927" "Don't let the Perez Park Security Chief down, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P444301767" "Take this briefing seriously.  I need you to deal with some of the Circle of Thorns mystics that have been plaguing the area.  Try looking for them in Bettis Hills."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P153117717" "Keep peace in Perez Park"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2240965719" "Deal with the Circle in Perez Park!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1032251960" "You have defeated 10 Circle of Thorns mystics."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1696648063" "I guess the Chief's confidence in you was well placed. Fantastic job, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3748397090" "Steel Canyon briefing"
// DetailString :
"P1442114520" "Steel Canyon is the financial district of Paragon City.  Many national banks, insurance companies, and investment firms have their headquarters in this zone.  In fact, so much money flows through Steel Canyon, Paragon City ranks among America's richest cities.  Success has spurred the construction of so many skyscrapers that the place looks like a canyon made of concrete, glass and metal.  The zone isn't without its dangers, though.  The Outcasts have claimed the area as their own, and they've recruited a lot of kids with mutant powers related to the elements.  That's what the Outcasts love best - beating down their enemies with the power of the elements."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1068792961" "There is trouble in Steel Canyon.  Get your assignment from the Security Chief."
// AcceptString :
"P1846062885" "Talk to the Steel Canyon Security Chief"
// SendOffString :
"P3294399530" "You will probably be dealing with the Outcasts, so be ready for anything."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3128820337" "Don't let the Security Chief down, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1579070171" "Here is some info on the area.  I need you to get out on the streets and contain the Outcasts.  They can usually be found in Blyde Square or the Copper District."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P297338366" "Keep peace in Steel Canyon"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1836800443" "Deal with the Outcasts for Security!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3767827999" "You have defeated 10 Outcasts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1486392681" "Well done; those Outcasts are a powerful bunch.  It seems the number of mutants in the city is increasing rapidly."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2077111962" "Boomtown briefing"
// DetailString :
"P2374113737" "Baumton was the city's first marketplace, where tradesman and farmers went to sell their wares.  After the Rikti Invasion, people started calling it Boomtown, because the devastation reminded them of a bomb crater.  <color orange>It's pretty dangerous. If I were you, I wouldn't go in without a few other heroes for backup.</color>  The place is infested with those Clockwork robots.  They look like toys, but they cause plenty of havoc by stealing bits of machinery and metal from all over.  Even worse, a giant clockwork monster called Babbage prevents any pacification of the zone.  Be especially careful of him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1953768717" "Lately, the Clockwork have been tearing Boomtown apart.  Report to the Security Chief for that zone and he will tell you what to do."
// AcceptString :
"P3236181629" "Talk to the Boomtown Security Chief"
// SendOffString :
"P2883092974" "I don't know why they do this, but the Clockwork are becoming more of a menace every day.  Watch out for the huge monster, Babbage!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_4_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2410423142" "Here is some info on Boomtown.  {HeroName}, I need you to stop the Clockwork!  You could start looking for them in Primer or the Cannonade."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_4_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P275718214" "Keep peace in Boomtown"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3963148644" "Deal with the Clockwork for Security!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1060572962" "You have defeated 10 Clockwork."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4067509488" "We used to laugh at the Clockwork.  Not anymore.  Well done, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1227226752" "Skyway City briefing"
// DetailString :
"P4099168690" "Back in the 1970's, there was a huge drive to create highways to relieve congestion in the city.  No one would need to drive on the surface streets - instead, we would drive above them!  So the city started building high spanning bridges everywhere, and Skyway City quickly turned into one big highway in sky.  Now this zone is home to a street gang that likes to camp out underneath bridges: the Trolls.  These are thugs who've mutated, thanks to taking a bit too much Superadine.  But watch out; the drug has given many of them inhuman strength and resistance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2589184833" "The Trolls are rampaging again!  The Security Chief asked for you by name.  Find him, and get your assignment."
// AcceptString :
"P2848655164" "Talk to the Skyway City Security Chief"
// SendOffString :
"P3890918349" "These rampages are happening more and more.  Something has to be done!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_5_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1205377823" "Take this and get on the streets immediately.  Stop those Trolls!  They've caused a lot of havoc in Vista Plaza and the Astral District."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_5_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2417346834" "Stop rampage in Skyway City"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1112576336" "Deal with the Trolls for Security!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P833359893" "You have stopped the rampage."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2001848232" "Good job today.  There must be some link between Superadine and these rampages.  The Trolls need to be cut off from their supply."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided_6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SCInstructions 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4100306626" "Hollows briefing"
// DetailString :
"P4264878296" "Eastgate used to be a nice residential neighborhood with a view of the ocean.  Before Trolls moved in, that is.  On a quest for more territory, a group of Trolls headed into the sewers under Eastgate with the intent of blasting open a large area.  What they didn't know was that there was already an extensive cave warren beneath the area.  Their blasts destabilized the ground and collapsed a large section of the zone.  When the dust settled, the surviving Trolls realized that they had found an excellent area for expansion.  This event became known as the Hollowing. Since the Hollowing, other groups have moved into the area, including the Outcasts, the Circle of Thorns, and the strange rock-like creatures known as Pumicites.  The Paragon City Police Department has its hands full trying to expel these threats so that reconstruction on the Hollows can begin.  <color orange>You might want to bring some friends, The Hollows is no place to be by yourself.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1453996152" "Have you heard about the Hollows, {HeroName}?  Ever since the Trolls moved into Eastgate, the Paragon PD has been fighting a losing battle against them. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you're willing, I'd like you to go talk to Lt. David Wincott of the Trolls Task Force.</a>  He could really use your help in reclaiming the Hollows.  Of course, we can really use your help here, too.  Wherever you'd like to lend a hand, you'll be welcome."
// AcceptString :
"P2015741443" "Talk to Lt. David Wincott"
// SendOffString :
"P2405158374" "The Trolls are the worst problem in the Hollows, but they aren't the only one.  I'll let Lt. Wincott fill you in."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2305317958" "Wincott's a good man who's had a hard time recently.  Do right by him, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4147258767" "Here's a briefing I wrote up for you.  It'll help you understand what Wincott's up against out there."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3309441047" "Ever since the Trolls kidnapped my son, Sam, four years ago, I've been dedicated to rooting them out of the Hollows.  But, let's face it: I need every bit of help I can get.  If you would like to help me, I'd be grateful. <br><br>Otherwise, you can keep pursuing leads with your current contacts. I'll still be here if you decide the fight for the Hollows is something you want to be a part of."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Guided7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2717007065" "This might interest you, {HeroName}.  Hero Corps have begun a new service to help Heroes who are looking for more difficult challenges.  You should talk to one of their Field Analysts and see if it interests you."
// AcceptString :
"P2914249091" "Speak to a Hero Corps Field Analyst"
// SendOffString :
"P1185680128" "Remember that this whole thing is completely optional.  You can ignore it if you like, but you should know about it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4294184018" "Speak to Hero Corp Analyst"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1564550963" "Remember that this whole Field Analyst thing is completely optional.  You can ignore it if you like, but you should know about it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4139096515" "Thank you for seeing me, {HeroName}.  Hero Corps is dedicated to helping all of the city's Heroes, and we're unveiling a new service to help you reach for the highest possible levels of achievement.  If you want to face more difficult foes and challenges than a Hero of your level normally would, let us know, and we'll get the word around to all of your contacts.  They'll make sure to give you the toughest assignments possible.  If you later decide that you'd like to tone your challenges back down to normal or take them even higher, you can always speak to one of our Field Analysts such as myself, and we'll be happy to help you change things either way. <br><br>Thanks for visiting with us, {HeroName}.  Remember that Hero Corps is here to help Heroes!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2051130058" "It's an interesting service, if you're looking for more difficult challenges.  It's completely optional, though, so don't worry about it if it doesn't interest you."
